{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"pwd && git status --short && sed -n '1,240p' <original-home>/.codex/skills/aristotle-cli/SKILL.md && rg -n -i -C 2 'P55A|local-hyperbolic|two-lane|aristotle closeout' <original-home>/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md\"","aggregated_output":"lean/stabilizer\n M PLAN.md\n M aristotle_tasks/P49-finite-corner-trace.md\n M aristotle_tasks/P50-normal-faithful-corner-trace.md\n M aristotle_tasks/P51-full-finite-corner-central-exclusion.md\n M aristotle_tasks/P55-regional-concrete-cstar-alpha.md\n M aristotle_tasks/P60-full-corner-semifinite-weight.md\n M work/TWO-LANE-FORMALIZATION-DECISION.md\n?? AristotleCandidates/FiniteCornerTrace.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/FullCornerSemifiniteWeight.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/FullFiniteCornerCentralExclusion.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/KaplanskyDensity.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/LocalHyperbolicAlgebraicAlpha.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/MixedUHFHyperfiniteFactor.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/NormalFaithfulCornerTrace.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/StrongOperatorClosedVonNeumann.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/UltraweakNormality.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/VonNeumannBicommutantTheorem.lean\n?? aristotle_tasks/P50U-ultraweak-normality-bridge.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P55A-local-hyperbolic-finite-stage-uhf-bridge.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P55B-local-hyperbolic-source-uhf-bridge.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P55C-local-hyperbolic-concrete-representations.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P55D-regional-concrete-cstar-alpha.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P60R-full-corner-standard-semifiniteness-repair.md\n?? reviews/P49-finite-corner-trace-closeout.md\n?? reviews/P49-finite-corner-trace-recovery.md\n?? reviews/P49A-strong-operator-closed-von-neumann-closeout.md\n?? reviews/P49B-von-neumann-bicommutant-theorem-closeout.md\n?? reviews/P49C-kaplansky-density-closeout.md\n?? reviews/P50-normal-faithful-corner-trace-closeout-rerun.md\n?? reviews/P50-normal-faithful-corner-trace-closeout.md\n?? reviews/P50-normal-faithful-corner-trace-recovery.md\n?? reviews/P50U-ultraweak-normality-bridge-closeout.md\n?? reviews/P51-full-finite-corner-central-exclusion-closeout.md\n?? reviews/P51-full-finite-corner-central-exclusion-recovery.md\n?? reviews/P53-local-hyperbolic-algebraic-alpha-closeout.md\n?? reviews/P55-regional-concrete-cstar-alpha-out-of-budget.md\n?? reviews/P58-mixed-uhf-hyperfinite-factor-closeout.md\n?? reviews/P60-full-corner-semifinite-weight-closeout.md\n---\nname: aristotle-cli\ndescription: Use when Codex should interact with the Aristotle CLI to submit Lean projects or papers, request sorry filling or formalization runs, inspect job status, and download results for iterative project work.\n---\n\n# Aristotle CLI\n\nUse Aristotle for remote Lean/project runs when the local repo is ready but needs automated proof search, sorry filling, or formalization help.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Confirm the target project or paper from the current workspace.\n2. Check the local build or project state first. Prefer a narrow local `lake build` or equivalent before submitting anything remote.\n3. Use the bundled wrapper `scripts/aristotle-auth.sh` unless `ARISTOTLE_API_KEY` is already known to be exported in the current process.\n4. Submit the smallest useful task prompt. Keep it concrete and tied to the files at hand.\n5. Wait for the result when that is useful. Otherwise poll or list jobs.\n6. Download artifacts, inspect the diffs, and rerun local verification.\n\n## Commands\n\nUse the commands in [references/aristotle-cli.md](references/aristotle-cli.md).\n\n## Operating rules\n\n- Prefer `aristotle submit` for Lean project work, especially sorry filling or proof search.\n- Prefer `aristotle formalize` when the input is a paper or TeX source that should become a Lean artifact.\n- Use `aristotle list` to inspect recent jobs and `aristotle download` to retrieve results.\n- Keep prompts specific: name the file, theorem, section, or proof obligation instead of asking for broad improvement.\n- If a run fails, inspect the local artifact and re-submit only after the prompt or project state is corrected.\n- Do not print or log the API key.\n- If authentication fails but `~/.bashrc` contains the key, do not assume sourcing `.bashrc` works. Many `.bashrc` files return early for noninteractive shells. Use `scripts/aristotle-auth.sh`.\n\n## When to escalate back to the user\n\n- The CLI is missing, or authentication still fails after trying `scripts/aristotle-auth.sh`.\n- The target repo is not a Lean project or paper and needs clarification.\n- The requested action would overwrite user work outside the target project tree.\n292-- symptom: `git diff --check` reports broad generated-file whitespace noise -> fix: run a focused check on the changed CSS files and leave unrelated worktree dirt untouched. [Task 1]\n293-\n294:# Task Group: source-workspace two-lane Aristotle/Codex formalization autopilot\n295-\n296:scope: autonomous two-lane theorem formalization, terminal-status Codex closeout, safe artifact staging, and resource-bounded Lean verification\n297-applies_to: cwd=source-workspace; reuse_rule=reuse only after checking the live queues, `state.json`, systemd unit, Lean checkout, and Aristotle task state; no acceptance or advancement is implied by this partial rollout\n298-\n--\n301-### rollout_summary_files\n302-\n303:- rollout_summaries/2026-08-06T14-29-28-EPRR-two_lane_aristotle_autopilot_closeout_hardening.md (cwd=source-workspace, rollout_path=<original-home>/.codex/sessions/2026/08/06/rollout-2026-08-06T16-29-28-019fd77a-ab18-78f3-a38a-968e45471677.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-06T18:07:30+00:00, thread_id=019fd77a-ab18-78f3-a38a-968e45471677, success: two-lane queues and compact manuscript staging verified)\n304-\n305-### keywords\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' AGENTS.md && sed -n '1,300p' PLAN.md && sed -n '1,280p' work/TWO-LANE-FORMALIZATION-DECISION.md && sed -n '1,320p' aristotle_tasks/P55A-local-hyperbolic-finite-stage-uhf-bridge.md && rg --files -g 'PROGRESS.md' -g 'STATE.md' -g '*HANDOFF*' -g '*status*' -g 'SOURCE-CONTRACT.md' -g 'CONTEXT-LEDGER.md' -g 'lakefile.lean' -g 'lean-toolchain' | sort && printf '\\\\n-- quarantine/archive --\\\\n' && ls -ld aristotle_responses/P55A-local-hyperbolic-finite-stage-uhf-bridge-1ac3c887-2e89017e-quarantine aristotle_responses/P55A-local-hyperbolic-finite-stage-uhf-bridge-1ac3c887-2e89017e.tar.gz && tar -tzf aristotle_responses/P55A-local-hyperbolic-finite-stage-uhf-bridge-1ac3c887-2e89017e.tar.gz\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' AGENTS.md && sed -n '1,300p' PLAN.md && sed -n '1,280p' work/TWO-LANE-FORMALIZATION-DECISION.md && sed -n '1,320p' aristotle_tasks/P55A-local-hyperbolic-finite-stage-uhf-bridge.md && rg --files -g 'PROGRESS.md' -g 'STATE.md' -g '*HANDOFF*' -g '*status*' -g 'SOURCE-CONTRACT.md' -g 'CONTEXT-LEDGER.md' -g 'lakefile.lean' -g 'lean-toolchain' | sort && printf '\\\\n-- quarantine/archive --\\\\n' && ls -ld aristotle_responses/P55A-local-hyperbolic-finite-stage-uhf-bridge-1ac3c887-2e89017e-quarantine aristotle_responses/P55A-local-hyperbolic-finite-stage-uhf-bridge-1ac3c887-2e89017e.tar.gz && tar -tzf aristotle_responses/P55A-local-hyperbolic-finite-stage-uhf-bridge-1ac3c887-2e89017e.tar.gz\"","aggregated_output":"# Manuscript-Only Context Policy\n\n## Source authority\n\nFor manuscript-facing statements, the sole mathematical source is\n`sources/manuscript/main.tex`.\nThe local summary and locator record is `SOURCE-CONTRACT.md`. Do not modify\nthe manuscript from this project.\n\nEvery claim described as coming from the manuscript must identify an exact\nline range in `main.tex`. Repository history, earlier chat context, and other\nartifacts are not substitute sources.\n\n## Context firewall\n\nDo not introduce, assume, or attribute to the manuscript any gLU,\nrefinement, layer-coherence, or finite-coordinate construction unless it is\npresent in the cited manuscript lines or is explicitly introduced as a new\nauxiliary assumption. A Lean file compiling does not make its unstated\nphysical or operator-algebraic hypotheses part of the manuscript.\n\nClassify each item as one of:\n\n1. **manuscript-derived**: exact source locator and no stronger conclusion;\n2. **auxiliary assumption**: explicitly labelled and used only conditionally;\n3. **Lean infrastructure**: reusable formal mathematics that makes no source\n   claim; or\n4. **legacy exploratory work**: retained for reference but unavailable as\n   support for a manuscript-derived assertion.\n\n`CONTEXT-LEDGER.md` records the current legacy items.\n\n## Current formalization boundary\n\nThe target discussed in the manuscript is the short-range regional-algebra\nstatement at `main.tex:1740-1752`; its proposed proof is at\n`main.tex:1891-2004`. Keep separate the asserted algebraic identification,\nthe product-state/GNS steps, the unformalized operator-algebraic completion and\nspatial tensor-product steps, and the trace conclusion. A tracial state is\nappropriate only for the finite pure-sector case. The infinite pure-sector\ntarget instead calls for a faithful normal semifinite trace/weight when the\nrequired hypotheses and von Neumann infrastructure are supplied.\n\n## Aristotle task packets\n\nEvery new task under `aristotle_tasks/` must begin with exactly one context\ndeclaration:\n\n- `Source basis: main.tex:<line range>` for a manuscript-facing task; or\n- `Infrastructure only:` for reusable Lean material that makes no manuscript\n  claim.\n\nIt must then list every auxiliary assumption, state its exact Lean target, and\nsay whether its conclusion is conditional. A task may not cite a legacy\nartifact as its source basis. Use `aristotle_tasks/TEMPLATE.md` for new\npackets.\n\n## Active two-lane plan execution\n\nThe active Codex/Aristotle execution plan is `PLAN.md`, with the approval\nrecord in `work/TWO-LANE-FORMALIZATION-DECISION.md`. Before starting any new\npackage in the P47--P61 program, read both files and the closeout/audit record\nfor every declared predecessor.\n\nEvery future packet must include a `Plan alignment` section containing:\n\n1. the exact package identifier and its lane: `G` (general finite-corner and\n   central type-III exclusion), `H` (explicit local-hyperbolic tensor-factor\n   model), `shared`, or `reconnection`;\n2. the predecessor packages that have already been integrated, or `none` for\n   a foundation package;\n3. the exact gate this package is permitted to discharge; and\n4. downstream claims it is forbidden to make.\n\nThe Aristotle prompt must explicitly instruct the worker to read the active\nplan and respect this section. A package may use only integrated, compiled\npredecessors; a finished remote job is not a dependency until it has passed\nthe local semantic audit. Do not infer a theorem from a later package, and do\nnot submit a dependent packet before its listed prerequisites are integrated.\n\nFor Lane G, the required conclusion is a nonzero finite **projection** in\nevery nonzero central summand; a finite-dimensional subalgebra is not enough.\nFor Lane H, do not call the local algebra a factor until the spatial tensor\nfactorization and factorhood of both factors are proved. Neither lane may\nclaim a global trace/weight unless it constructs or explicitly assumes one.\n\n## Verification and reporting\n\nReport Lean compilation separately from mathematical validation. For each\nmanuscript-facing milestone, state which source clauses are represented, which\nassumptions remain external, and which analytic/von Neumann-algebraic claims\nare not yet formalized in the pinned Mathlib version.\n# Active plan: two-lane stabilizer-algebra formalization\n\n## Decision — 2026-08-07\n\nThe project now has two parallel mathematical targets sharing finite\nstabilizer and operator-algebra infrastructure, but neither is allowed to\nsilently supply the other one's hypotheses.\n\n### Lane G — general lattices and central type-III exclusion\n\n**Source basis:** `main.tex:332-342`, with the corner proof at\n`main.tex:1026-1536`.\n\nFor a general consistent stabilizer system and region, construct the decreasing\nlocal-code projection tower, its strong limit `q`, and the finite corner\n`q M_Gamma q`. Prove that the vector functional `tau_q` is a faithful normal\ntracial **state** on that corner, hence that `q` is finite; prove `q` is full;\nand derive that every nonzero central projection `z` has `zq != 0` finite in\n`z M_Gamma`. Conclude that no nonzero central summand is type III.\n\nThis lane does **not** require a direct-integral formalization or a global\ntrace/weight on `M_Gamma`. A global faithful normal semifinite weight is a\nseparate optional strengthening. The condition to formalize is the existence\nof a nonzero finite **projection/corner** in each nonzero central summand, not\nmerely a finite-dimensional subalgebra.\n\n### Lane H — explicit local-hyperbolic tensor-factor model\n\n**Source basis:** `main.tex:1671-1679`, `main.tex:1898-2004`.\n\nFrom a coherent local hyperbolic basis, construct the finite coordinate maps,\ntheir coherent algebraic direct-limit star equivalence, concrete C-star\nmodels, the state identity, and the product GNS tensor splitting. Then prove\nthe special regional algebra is spatially isomorphic to\n\n`B(K_pure) barTensor R_mixed`.\n\nAfter proving the two factors and their spatial tensor product, derive the\ntrivial-center/factor conclusion for this special case. This conclusion does\nnot follow merely from the word \"hyperbolic\"; it follows from the constructed\nspatial factorization.\n\n### Reconnection\n\nLane H gives an explicit factor theorem and, in the infinite-pure case, the\nconcrete faithful normal semifinite weight `Tr barTensor tau`. Lane G gives\nthe general no-central-type-III theorem. A final comparison theorem may show\nthat the Lane-H factor model satisfies the Lane-G finite-corner criterion, but\nthe two results remain logically independent.\n\n## Aristotle package sequence\n\n### Shared/central core\n\n| Packet | Lean target | Purpose and acceptance gate |\n|---|---|---|\n| P47 | `CenterFiniteProjectionCore.lean` | Define center, central projections, finite projections, corners, central support, and fullness for the concrete von Neumann-algebra model. Prove only algebraic order/corner lemmas; no direct integral. |\n| P48 | `GeneralLatticeProjectionTower.lean` | Formalize the general-lattice exhaustion, local code projections, monotonicity, and the strong-limit projection `q`. If the stabilizer definitions do not imply a required limit fact, expose it as an auxiliary hypothesis. |\n| P49 | `FiniteCornerTrace.lean` | Derive finite-stage trace cyclicity and pass it to the compressed quasi-local C-star algebra. Keep finite codespace density data explicit. |\n| P49A | `StrongOperatorClosedVonNeumann.lean` | Develop the strong-operator convergence/closure API needed for concrete operator algebras; prove commutants and hence concrete von Neumann algebras are strongly closed. This is a proved infrastructure theorem, not an interface. |\n| P49B | `VonNeumannBicommutantTheorem.lean` | Prove the analytic double-commutant theorem for a unital complex star subalgebra of bounded operators: its bicommutant is its strong-operator closure. Develop the required finite amplification/cyclic-subspace machinery locally when Mathlib lacks it. |\n| P49C | `KaplanskyDensity.lean` | Prove bounded/unit-ball Kaplansky density for the represented C-star algebra in its bicommutant and derive the compressed-corner approximation used by the manuscript. No supplied density interface is accepted. |\n| P50 | `NormalFaithfulCornerTrace.lean` | Using P49 and P49C, prove traciality of `tau_q` on `q M_Gamma q` by bounded strong approximation, prove faithfulness, and establish the stronger concrete WOT-continuity certificate that P50U will translate into the standard ultraweak-normal interface. |\n| P50U | `UltraweakNormality.lean` | Define the concrete ultraweak topology from absolutely summable matrix-coefficient series, prove the ultraweak-to-WOT identity is continuous, and upgrade P50's WOT-continuity certificate to literal ultraweak normality. This is mandatory infrastructure and may not alias ultraweak topology to WOT/SOT/norm. |\n| P51 | `FullFiniteCornerCentralExclusion.lean` | Prove `q` finite, prove fullness, and derive `0 != z ->` a nonzero finite projection in `z M_Gamma`; define/use the project-local type-III obstruction. |\n\n### Explicit local-hyperbolic lane\n\n| Packet | Lean target | Purpose and acceptance gate |\n|---|---|---|\n| P52 | `CoherentLocalHyperbolicCoordinates.lean` | Build finite coordinate blocks and an exhaustion from local hyperbolic data. Audit whether finite support suffices; otherwise isolate the exact local-finiteness/coherence assumption. |\n| P53 | `LocalHyperbolicAlgebraicAlpha.lean` | Construct the finite stage maps, phase calibration, and coherent algebraic `alpha`; instantiate the existing direct-limit theorems without supplied stage equivalences. |\n| P54 | `UHFReferenceRepresentation.lean` | Construct a faithful compatible Hilbert/operator representation of the dyadic algebra from finite stages; do not assume an infinite tensor-product Hilbert space. |\n| P55A | `LocalHyperbolicFiniteStageUHFBridge.lean` | Construct, rather than assume, the finite-stage star equivalence from each P53 coordinate Pauli algebra to the corresponding finite dyadic matrix algebra, with explicit generator/phase formulas and norm control. |\n| P55B | `LocalHyperbolicSourceUHFBridge.lean` | Prove coherence of the P55A maps and identify the P53 source direct limit with the coordinate dyadic limit; prove the finite terminal-stage and infinite cofinal-UHF branches separately. |\n| P55C | `LocalHyperbolicConcreteRepresentations.lean` | Transport the P54 faithful representation through P55B and P53 alpha, and construct the source and regional closed operator-range C-star algebras with faithful dense embeddings. |\n| P55D | `RegionalConcreteCStarAlpha.lean` | Extend the P53 algebraic alpha uniquely between the P55C concrete C-star closures and prove the inverse and dense-range identities. |\n| P56 | `RegionalProductStateIdentity.lean` | After P55D, prove the stabilizer/product-state equality on finite Pauli words and extend it by density and continuity. |\n| P57 | `ProductGNSTensorFactorization.lean` | Construct the pure/mixed product GNS Hilbert-space tensor splitting and the spatial represented-algebra identification. |\n| P58 | `MixedUHFHyperfiniteFactor.lean` | Construct/prove the finite mixed matrix and infinite mixed hyperfinite-II1 alternatives under project-local factor and normal-trace definitions. |\n| P59 | `LocalHyperbolicFactorTraceTheorem.lean` | Transport P57--P58 to the regional algebra, prove trivial center, and state the finite-pure trace versus infinite-pure faithful-normal-semifinite-weight dichotomy. |\n\n### Optional strengthening/reconnection\n\n| Packet | Lean target | Purpose |\n|---|---|---|\n| P60 | `FullCornerSemifiniteWeight.lean` | Retired partial attempt: it constructs a conditional extended-positive trace series and finite-compression certificate, but does not yet prove standard positive-cone semifiniteness. |\n| P60R | `FullCornerSemifiniteWeight.lean` | Recovery: define the weight on the positive cone and prove standard semifiniteness using positive square roots and the finite comparison projections. |\n| P61 | `HyperbolicImpliesCentralCriterion.lean` | Show the explicit Lane-H model supplies the finite-corner criterion used by Lane G. |\n\n## Initial parallel wave\n\nSubmit only the four independent foundation packets first: P47, P48, P52,\nand P54. Integrate and semantically audit them before submitting dependent\npackets. Existing P42--P46 task drafts are preserved as historical drafts;\nthey are not evidence and must be re-scoped against this plan before reuse.\n\n## Non-negotiable gates\n\n1. No claim that `q M_Gamma q` has merely a semifinite weight when the\n   construction actually targets a finite faithful normal tracial state.\n2. No claim of a global trace/weight on `M_Gamma` from the finite-corner\n   theorem alone.\n3. No claim that a finite-dimensional subalgebra excludes type III; the proof\n   must produce a nonzero finite projection in every nonzero central summand.\n4. No claim that hyperbolic data imply a factor before the spatial tensor\n   factorization and factorhood of both factors are proved.\n5. Every manuscript-facing packet identifies an exact `main.tex` locator and\n   every extra analytic hypothesis appears as a named field, never an axiom.\n6. P49A--P49C are mandatory proved infrastructure. P50 may not replace the\n   bicommutant theorem or Kaplansky density by a supplied structure field; an\n   incomplete analytic package halts Lane G and triggers review.\n7. P50's WOT-continuity theorem is a mathematically stronger certificate but\n   is not itself the standard definition of normality. P50U must formalize the\n   actual ultraweak topology and checked comparison before the project reports\n   the corner state as ultraweak-normal in the formal interface. P51's\n   finiteness/fullness proof is logically independent because it uses only\n   traciality and faithfulness.\n8. The original P55 exhausted its remote budget without producing its\n   authorized Lean file. It is retired, not accepted. P55A--P55D replace it\n   and expose the previously missing bridge between P53's twisted-Pauli direct\n   limit and P54's dyadic UHF model. P56 may advance only after P55D is\n   integrated and audited.\n\n---\n\n# Previous single-lane plan: retained background\n\n## Objective\n\nFormalize, from the manuscript's actual finite-support adapted-coordinate data,\na state-preserving C-star isomorphism from the quasi-local Pauli algebra to the\nregional algebra.  Obtain the represented von Neumann algebra equivalence by\nthe canonical GNS unitary, then apply an independently established product\nfactor classification.\n\nThe source basis is exclusively `SOURCE-CONTRACT.md` and the cited manuscript\nlocators.  In particular, no gLU/refinement/layer-coherence premise is allowed\nunless later added explicitly as a new auxiliary assumption.\n\n## Current position\n\nThe project already has checked conditional interfaces for:\n\n1. finite Pauli/stabilizer coordinates and pure/mixed states;\n2. algebraic direct limits, their induced algebraic equivalence `alpha`, and\n   compatible state transport;\n3. supplied C-star completions and a supplied C-star extension of `alpha`;\n4. GNS transport for supplied compatible C-star states; and\n5. supplied normal/product-factor transport.\n\nThese are scaffolding.  They do not discharge the manuscript-specific finite\ncoordinate construction or the product-factor classification.\n\n## Phase A — exact finite coordinate theorem\n\n**Goal:** Replace abstract finite-stage star equivalences by maps constructed\nfrom a finite restriction of the adapted symplectic basis.\n\n1. Specify a finite region/exhaustion and the finite Pauli label spaces.\n2. Define the coordinate map from the adapted `z_i,x_i` data.\n3. Prove the Pauli multiplier and star equations, including the required phase\n   correction.\n4. Prove the map is a finite-stage complex star-algebra equivalence.\n5. Prove its stabilizer membership criterion and the finite product-state\n   expectation formula.\n\n**Gate A:** no supplied finite-stage star equivalence remains in the finite\nmanuscript theorem; only explicitly stated finite adapted-coordinate data does.\n\n## Phase B — coherence and quasi-local C-star isomorphism\n\n**Goal:** Construct the actual C-star isomorphism `alpha`, rather than assume\nan algebraic or completed extension.\n\n1. Prove the Phase-A maps commute exactly with all finite-region inclusions.\n2. Form the algebraic direct-limit star equivalence.\n3. Specify the quasi-local C-star completions as inductive-limit completions.\n4. Prove the algebraic map is isometric on the dense quasi-local subalgebras.\n5. Extend it uniquely to a C-star star-algebra equivalence\n   `alpha : P_quasilocal ≃⋆ₐ[ℂ] A_regional`.\n\n**Gate B:** P23 and P25 are instantiated by proved data, not used as supplied\ninterfaces.\n\n## Phase C — state identity and GNS transport\n\n**Goal:** Prove the regional state pulled back by `alpha` is the pure/mixed\nproduct state.\n\n1. Check equality on finite Pauli-word bases using Phase A's stabilizer\ncriterion.\n2. Prove compatibility under inclusions and hence equality on the quasi-local\nC-star algebra by density/continuity.\n3. Instantiate the existing C-star/GNS bridge to obtain the canonical GNS\nunitary and its intertwining identity.\n4. Use conjugation by that unitary to identify the represented von Neumann\nalgebras.\n\n**Gate C:** do not use a separate quasi-equivalence/normal-folium argument.\nIt is unnecessary once the state-preserving C-star isomorphism is proved.\n\n## Phase D — product representation classification\n\n**Goal:** Independently prove or source the product-state representation\ntheorem.\n\n1. Split coordinate indices into pure and mixed sectors.\n2. Establish the infinite-product GNS factorization.\n3. Identify the pure sector as `B(K_pure)`.\n4. Identify the mixed sector as a finite matrix factor when finite, or the\nhyperfinite `II_1` factor when infinite.\n5. Establish the spatial tensor-product identification of the product\nrepresentation.\n\n**Gate D:** every analytic theorem is either formalized against a supported\nMathlib API or recorded as an exact external theorem with source locator and\nexplicit hypothesis.\n\n## Phase E — theorem and trace corollaries\n\n1. Transport the Phase-D product classification through the Phase-C GNS\nunitary to the regional von Neumann algebra.\n2. State the finite-pure and infinite-pure cases separately.\n3. Finite pure sector: derive the normalized tracial-state conclusion.\n4. Infinite pure sector: state the faithful normal semifinite trace/weight\nconclusion; do not call it a tracial state.\n5. Audit every conclusion against `main.tex:1740-1752` and record any required\nmanuscript correction separately.\n\n## Parallelization\n\nUntil Phase B is blocked on a single coherent-coordinate construction, run in\nparallel:\n\n- finite phase/cocycle verification;\n- finite adapted-coordinate/stabilizer-state verification;\n- finite inclusion/coherence lemmas;\n- Mathlib/API feasibility audits for C-star inductive limits and GNS products;\n- product mixed-sector classification/source work.\n\nDo not parallelize mutually dependent attempts at the same global `alpha`.\nEach new Aristotle packet must use `aristotle_tasks/TEMPLATE.md` and state its\nsource basis plus every auxiliary assumption.\n\n## Exit criterion\n\nCall the manuscript theorem formally established only when Gates A--D are\ndischarged and Phase E compiles without substituting supplied interfaces for\nthe central finite-coordinate, C-star-extension, state-identity, or\nproduct-classification claims.\n# Two-lane formalization decision\n\nDate: 2026-08-07\n\nThe active Codex/Aristotle loop follows the two-lane plan in `PLAN.md`.\n\n**Lane G** formalizes the manuscript's general-lattice corner argument:\nthe strong-limit code projection `q`, the faithful normal finite tracial state\non `q M_Gamma q`, finiteness and fullness of `q`, and the conclusion that each\nnonzero central summand has a nonzero finite projection and hence is not type\nIII. This route does not use a direct integral and does not require a global\ntrace/weight on `M_Gamma`.\n\n**Lane H** formalizes the explicit short-range/local-hyperbolic model:\ncoherent coordinate maps, an algebraic and C-star `alpha`, the product-state\nidentity, product GNS tensor factorization, and the resulting factor and\ntrace/weight classification.\n\nThe lanes meet only after their own gates are met. In particular, the explicit\ntensor-factor result proves trivial center in the special local-hyperbolic\ncase, whereas the general corner result rules out type-III central summands\nwithout asserting trivial center.\n\nThe first approved parallel Aristotle wave is P47, P48, P52, and P54. No\ndependent packet should be submitted before its prerequisite results are\nintegrated and semantically audited.\n\nAmendment, 2026-08-07: the analytic passage from the compressed quasi-local\nC-star algebra to the von Neumann corner is mandatory project infrastructure.\nAfter P48, the loop must prove strong closedness of concrete von Neumann\nalgebras (P49A), the analytic double-commutant theorem (P49B), and Kaplansky\nunit-ball density with its compressed-corner corollary (P49C). P50 depends on\nboth the finite-stage/C-star trace P49 and the proved P49C result. These core\nanalytic theorems may require new local topology machinery, but may not be\nreplaced by axioms or supplied interfaces.\n\nAmendment, 2026-08-08: P50's checked WOT continuity is retained as a stronger\nconcrete certificate, but the field name alone is not accepted as a\nformalization of the standard ultraweak definition of normality. Package P50U\nmust define the ultraweak topology from absolutely summable series of matrix\ncoefficients, prove the topology comparison, and export an explicitly\nultraweak-normal P50 conclusion. This does not block P51's finite-projection\nargument, which uses the corner state's traciality and faithfulness rather than\nnormality.\n\nAmendment, 2026-08-08: the original P55 is retired after Aristotle returned\n`OUT_OF_BUDGET` without creating `RegionalConcreteCStarAlpha.lean`. The failed\nrun is not evidence and no code from it is integrated. Lane H now uses four\nseparate gates: P55A constructs finite-stage Pauli-to-dyadic equivalences,\nP55B proves coherence and the finite/infinite direct-limit identifications,\nP55C constructs faithful source/regional operator representations and their\nclosed ranges, and P55D extends the algebraic alpha by density. This split is\nmathematical: P53 and P54 did not yet contain an identification between their\ntwo different algebraic direct limits. P56 depends on accepted P55D.\n\nP60 may run independently of Lane H after P51 and P50U. It is optional Lane-G\nstrengthening and must use P50U's literal ultraweak-normal corner state. It may\nassume an explicitly named countable comparison family for the full corner,\nbut it may not infer a global weight from fullness alone or conceal the weight,\nnormality, faithfulness, traciality, or semifiniteness laws in an axiom.\n\nAmendment, 2026-08-08: P60 compiled and its conditional weight-series,\ntraciality, faithfulness, corner restriction, and finite-compression results\nare preserved, but P60 is not accepted as the optional global-weight theorem.\nThe closeout's P51 provenance objection was stale: P51 is accepted in\n`reviews/P51-full-finite-corner-central-exclusion-recovery.md`. The genuine\nremaining gap is standard semifiniteness on the positive cone. P60R may revise\nthe P60 candidate in place, but must prove that for each nonzero positive\n`x ∈ M` there is a nonzero positive `y ≤ x` of finite weight. It must construct\nthe required positive square-root/factorization argument from Mathlib or\nlocal proved C-star theory; that factorization may not be a new hypothesis.\n# P55A — finite-stage local-hyperbolic Pauli-to-dyadic bridge\n\n## Context declaration\n\n- **Infrastructure only:** construct the finite-dimensional bridge that was\n  missing between P53's coordinate Pauli stages and the standard dyadic matrix\n  stages. No completed manuscript claim is asserted here.\n\n## Plan alignment\n\n- **Package and lane:** `P55A`; Lane `H`.\n- **Predecessors:** `P53`, integrated and locally audited before submission.\n- **Gate discharged:** construct the finite-stage Pauli-to-dyadic star\n  equivalences and prove their norm and generator formulas.\n- **Forbidden downstream claims:** no direct-limit equivalence, C-star\n  completion, regional alpha, state identity, GNS tensor split, factor\n  classification, or trace/weight conclusion.\n\nRead `PLAN.md` and `work/TWO-LANE-FORMALIZATION-DECISION.md` before editing.\n\n## Mathematical target\n\nCreate only\n`AristotleCandidates/LocalHyperbolicFiniteStageUHFBridge.lean`.\n\nFor `A : LocalHyperbolicAlpha.AlphaData L I`, a stage `n`, a natural number\n`k`, and an explicit enumeration `e : A.Coord n ≃ Fin k`, construct a complex\n`StarAlgEquiv`\n\n`A.sourceStageUHFEquiv n e :\n  LocalHyperbolicAlpha.pauliAlgebra (A.sourceForm n) ≃⋆ₐ[ℂ]\n    QubitTensorPower k`.\n\nThe equivalence must be built from the explicit P53 Pauli-word basis and an\nexplicit enumeration parameter; the star equivalence itself may not be\nsupplied as a structure field. Also export a default specialization at\n`k = Nat.card (A.Coord n)` using a constructed finite enumeration. Define the\nstandard finite-qubit `X` and `Z` words in the\nrecursive `QubitTensorPower` model and prove the images of the P53 coordinate\n`Z` and `X` generators, including every convention-dependent fourth-root\nphase. Prove multiplication, star preservation, bijectivity, and the induced\nnorm/isometry statements. If an equivalent indexing of the dyadic matrix\nstage is technically required, construct and prove the exact equivalence to\n`QubitTensorPower (Nat.card (A.Coord n))` in this file.\n\n## Auxiliary assumptions\n\nNo finite-stage star equivalence, norm equality, word basis, or matrix-unit\nidentification may be assumed. Classical choice of an enumeration of a finite\ntype is allowed and must appear only as constructed data. If the recursive\nleft-versus-right tensor convention introduces a permutation or phase, expose\nand prove it rather than strengthening the theorem silently.\n\n## Files and imports\n\nCreate only\n`AristotleCandidates/LocalHyperbolicFiniteStageUHFBridge.lean`; import P53,\n`Formalization.DyadicTensorTower`, and the checked finite-coordinate norm\ncontrol modules as needed. Do not edit predecessor modules.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates.LocalHyperbolicFiniteStageUHFBridge` passes.\n- No `sorry`, `admit`, new axiom, or supplied stage equivalence is introduced.\n- The response prints the exact generator formulas and convention-dependent\n  phases, the exact verification command, and all remaining assumptions.\n- No direct-limit or downstream Lane-H conclusion is claimed.\nCONTEXT-LEDGER.md\nPROGRESS.md\nSOURCE-CONTRACT.md\nlakefile.lean\nlean-toolchain\n\n-- quarantine/archive --\nls: cannot access 'aristotle_responses/P55A-local-hyperbolic-finite-stage-uhf-bridge-1ac3c887-2e89017e-quarantine': No such file or directory\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 lev lev 430706 Aug  8 18:14 aristotle_responses/P55A-local-hyperbolic-finite-stage-uhf-bridge-1ac3c887-2e89017e.tar.gz\n","exit_code":2,"status":"failed"}}
