t-state\n  indicator is exactly the selected-Z condition: a pure coordinate has no X\n  exponent, and a mixed coordinate is the identity label.  Under an arbitrary\n  supplied adapted coordinate basis, that condition is literal membership in\n  the selected-Z stabilizer submodule.  The coherent direct-limit state theorem\n  has a corresponding selected-Z indicator form on source basis words.\n- `PCC-001` — a phase-corrected additive map of Pauli labels respects word\n  multiplication and star exactly when it satisfies explicit multiplier and\n  involution equations.  This isolates the cocycle data that symplecticity\n  alone does not supply.  The cross-algebra word-basis extension is now also\n  checked: its two compatibility equations and a specified Pauli-word basis\n  yield a genuine `StarAlgEquiv`.\n- `SCC-001` — the quotient of two multiplier phases is an additive character,\n  calibrating by an additive character preserves the multiplier equation, and\n  every additive character on a vector subspace extends to the ambient vector\n  space along a complementary subspace.  This is the exact algebraic\n  stabilizer-sign calibration: the finite-field character is self-conjugate,\n  and calibration preserves both Pauli-word compatibility equations.  The\n  concrete finite-support quadratic phase is now independently formalized;\n  relating it to the actual regional stabilizer convention remains separate.\n- QPR-001 — the explicit ZMod 4 finite-support quadratic refinement has its\n  polarization and diagonal identities fully checked.  Its discrepancy pairing\n  is additive in both words, symmetric for a symmetric discrepancy, and has\n  additive order two.  These facts instantiate the cross-algebra Pauli-word\n  multiplication and involution certificates and, with a supplied word-basis\n  linear equivalence, a `StarAlgEquiv`.\n- QPT-001 — the concrete finite-support phase theorem now composes that\n  `StarAlgEquiv` with the finite-pure times qubit-UHF trace transport: whenever\n  the regional Pauli-word exponents, involution phases, and word-basis map are\n  supplied, Lean constructs both the star-algebra equivalence and its induced\n  algebraic tracial state with the elementary-tensor product formula.  The\n  Pauli-word interface has been weakened from `Ring` to `Semiring`, the exact\n  structure carried by the concrete algebraic UHF direct limit.\n- PTO-001 — two isometries whose range projections sum to the identity rule\n  out even an algebraic unital cyclic trace.  This is the checked obstruction\n  behind the infinite-pure-sector case; the tracial-state theorem is therefore\n  deliberately limited to a finite pure matrix factor.\n- ALT-001 — compatible finite-stage `StarAlgEquiv`s and compatible target\n  algebraic tracial states induce a source-side algebraic tracial state on the\n  corresponding quasi-local direct limit.  The theorem evaluates it exactly\n  on every finite-stage representative.  The concrete finite-pure UHF trace\n  now has the matching finite-stage elementary-tensor formula.\n- FQP-001 — every finite stage of the dyadic qubit tower now has an explicit\n  ordered Pauli-word `StarSystem` and a complex Pauli-word basis.  The\n  identity-qubit embeddings preserve its words, basis vectors, multiplication\n  multipliers, and star multipliers under coherent label maps.  Thus the UHF\n  target-side finite-stage word hypotheses are no longer abstract assumptions;\n  assembling them into one global target word system remains open.\n- PMS-001 — for every Boolean sequence specifying whether each newly adjoined\n  qubit is pure or maximally mixed, the corresponding finite product\n  functionals are algebraic states, are compatible with all dyadic embeddings,\n  and induce an algebraic state on the UHF direct limit.  Their values on every\n  finite Pauli word are proved recursively: pure coordinates permit only zero\n  X exponent, while mixed coordinates permit only the identity word.  The\n  all-mixed specialization is proved equal to the previously checked UHF\n  tracial state.  Lean also proves that even the one-qubit pure specialization\n  is not cyclic and hence not an algebraic tracial state.\n- PTR-001 — this nontraciality is now proved at arbitrary finite and\n  direct-limit coordinates: if any Boolean coordinate is pure, explicit\n  matrix units witness a failure of cyclicity.  Consequently the algebraic\n  UHF product state is tracial if and only if every coordinate is maximally\n  mixed, in which case it is the checked UHF trace.\n- CBL-001 — finite-stage star-algebra equivalences need not be assumed\n  coherent on every algebra element: if the source connecting maps, target\n  vectors, and coordinate maps agree on a specified source basis, Lean proves\n  the full commuting square by linear-basis extensionality.\n- CPS-001 — a phase-corrected finite coordinate system now has a concrete\n  direct-limit state interface.  Coherent source basis transport, phases, and\n  finite Pauli labels imply full-stage equivalence coherence and hence a\n  star-algebra equivalence to the algebraic qubit-UHF direct limit; the induced\n  source state evaluates a basis word as its phase times the pure/mixed Pauli\n  selection indicator.  The all-mixed specialization pulls the UHF trace back\n  to a source algebraic tracial state; more generally its pure/mixed pullback\n  is tracial exactly when every coordinate is mixed.  Constructing the\n  regional inputs remains open.\n- ACS-001 — if supplied finite-stage regional data identify selected target\n  Z-coordinates with the actual source stabilizer words, Lean derives the\n  exact phase-calibrated stabilizer expectation formula on every source basis word.\n  The stronger form states that hypothesis as literal membership in the\n  selected-Z submodule of an adapted coordinate basis.  Thus the remaining\n  geometric work is isolated to constructing and coherently transporting that\n  coordinate data from a separately supplied finite-coordinate realization,\n  rather than to a hidden infinite-algebra assumption. The manuscript does not\n  presently supply that realization; see `SOURCE-CONTRACT.md`.\n- ALS-001 — compatible finite-stage star-algebra equivalences transport\n  compatible algebraic states (not only tracial states) to a quasi-local\n  algebraic direct limit.  This is the exact state-level interface required by\n  a coherent regional stabilizer-coordinate construction.\n- WBE-001 — if Pauli words form a complex linear basis, checking a\n  complex-linear map on every pair of basis words proves multiplicativity on\n  all finite sums.  The corresponding conjugate-linear basis argument proves\n  star preservation; a bijective unital map satisfying both checks is packaged\n  as a star-algebra equivalence.\n- ALC-001 — a compatible family of finite-stage star-algebra maps induces a\n  star-algebra map from the algebraic directed limit.  Compatible finite-stage\n  star-algebra equivalences induce a star-algebra equivalence of the two\n  algebraic limits.  The C-star norm extension remains open.\n- CSE-001 — once a source and target are supplied as complex C-star algebras,\n  Lean proves that every complex `StarAlgEquiv` is isometric and therefore\n  continuous with continuous inverse.  A continuous target functional pulls\n  back continuously along it.  This does not construct C-star norms or\n  completions for the algebraic direct-limit models.\n- CCF-001 — the pinned Mathlib supports the finite dyadic stages as genuine\n  C-star algebras and supports closure/minimality once an ambient C-star\n  algebra is supplied.  It does not provide the C-star inductive-limit\n  construction for the algebraic dyadic limit; this is recorded as an\n  explicit missing API rather than hidden behind an axiom.\n- NMC-001 — supplied finite C-star realizations of the coherent coordinate\n  maps are isometric and continuous, and the commuting inclusion squares\n  preserve the norm estimates.  The resulting dense-subalgebra estimate is\n  exactly the analytic input needed before extending the algebraic map to a\n  completion; no completion is constructed here.\n- BMC-001 — for a star subalgebra of bounded operators on a Hilbert space,\n  Lean now constructs the algebraic bicommutant as a concrete\n  `VonNeumannAlgebra`, with monotonicity, minimality, membership, and\n  idempotence lemmas.  The analytic strong/weak double-commutant theorem is\n  still explicitly absent from the pinned Mathlib and remains separate.\n- CCC-001 — from an explicitly supplied isometric star representation of a\n  pre-C-star algebra into bounded operators, Lean constructs the closed\n  operator-range C-star algebra, its isometric dense embedding, and the\n  uniqueness equivalence between two such concrete completions.  The faithful\n  operator representation of the project-specific algebraic limit is still a\n  separate obligation.\n\n## The exact theorem still to prove\n\nThe Overleaf short-range theorem asserts a regional von Neumann algebra\nisomorphism to a type-I factor tensor a hyperfinite type-II1 factor.  It is\nnot yet formalized as a theorem because the supplied manuscript proof leaves\nthe following essential premises open:\n\n1. a finite-support adapted symplectic coordinate map whose finite-stage\n   source bases, phase correction, and target Pauli labels are coherent along\n   an exhaustion;\n2. identification of the actual regional Pauli multiplier and involution\n   exponents with the finite-support coordinate discrepancy, followed by\n   calibration to the actual stabilizer character;\n3. the induced quasi-local C-star isomorphism;\n4. factorization of the regional state into pure and normalized-tracial\n   coordinate states; and\n5. a normal/spatial extension to the respective bicommutants.\n\nThe current pinned mathlib version includes preliminary abstract and concrete\nvon Neumann-algebra definitions, but lacks a finished API for infinite von\nNeumann tensor products, normal states/traces, hyperfiniteness, and factor\nclassification.  The project therefore does not introduce any axiom for the\ntarget theorem.\n\n## Last verification\n\n```text\nlake build\nlake build Formalization.AlgebraicLimitStateTransport Formalization.QubitMatrixState Formalization.FinitePureMixedQubitState Formalization\nlake build Formalization.TraceTransport Formalization\nlake build Formalization.CoherentBasisEquiv Formalization.CoherentPhaseQubitState Formalization\nlake build Formalization.PureCoordinateNotTracial Formalization\nlake build Formalization.AdaptedStabilizerSubspace Formalization\nlake build Formalization.FiniteQubitPauliSelection Formalization.CoherentPhaseQubitState Formalization\nlake build Formalization.CStarEquivExtension Formalization\nlake build AristotleCandidates.CStarInductiveLimitFeasibility AristotleCandidates.FiniteCoordinateMapNormControl\nlake env lean /tmp/stabilizer_hyperfinite_axioms_run4.lean\npdflatex -interaction=nonstopmode -halt-on-error .../001-tensor-product-trace.tex\n```\n\nLean reports only `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound` for the\nchecked tensor-amplification, concrete dyadic direct-limit trace,\nfinite-support quadratic-phase, induced-trace, finite-qubit Pauli-word,\npure/mixed product-state, basis-level coherence, phase-corrected direct-limit\nequivalence/state transport, and properly-infinite trace-obstruction theorems.\nNo source theorem contains `sorry`, `admit`, or a user-declared axiom.  The\nblueprint build output is kept under `/tmp`, not in this source project.\n# Context ledger\n\n## Legacy exploratory material: not manuscript authority\n\nThe following artifacts contain gLU, refinement, or layer-coherence language\nimported from broader repository history rather than from the manuscript named\nin `SOURCE-CONTRACT.md`:\n\n- `blueprints/002-aristotle-parallel-formalization.tex`;\n- `aristotle_tasks/P6-layered-direct-limit.md`;\n- `AristotleCandidates/LayeredDirectLimit.lean`;\n- `AristotleCandidates/RegionalWitness.lean`; and\n- `Formalization/CoherentPhaseQubitState.lean`.\n\nThey are preserved unchanged as useful exploratory or infrastructure work.\nThey may be cited only by a future task explicitly marked `Infrastructure\nonly`; they cannot establish a manuscript-derived hypothesis or conclusion.\n\n## Interpretation rule\n\nWhen an older document conflicts with `AGENTS.md` or `SOURCE-CONTRACT.md`, the\nnew manuscript-only policy governs all future task packets and reports. No\nhistorical label retroactively changes the source basis of a checked Lean\ntheorem.\n# Manuscript source contract\n\n## Authoritative source\n\n- Manuscript: `sources/manuscript/main.tex`\n- Title in source: *Infinite Magic and the Continuum* (`main.tex:117`)\n- Formalization policy: `AGENTS.md`\n\nThis project does not treat its own Lean files, prior agent prompts, or the\nsurrounding repository as mathematical source authority.\n\n## Source clauses in scope\n\n| Source locator | What the manuscript says | Formalization status |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `main.tex:1671-1679` | Defines short-range order through a local symplectic basis, with `W_Gamma = span{z_i : i in P}` and finite support. | Requires a precise Lean model of the infinite Pauli/symplectic data. |\n| `main.tex:1740-1752` | States the short-range regional-algebra theorem, with an asserted factorization `A_Gamma` into a pure-sector type-I factor and a core factor that is finite type I or hyperfinite `II_1`. | Target statement; not established by current Lean artifacts. |\n| `main.tex:1915-1920` | Proposes an adapted symplectic basis and a star-isomorphism from an infinite Pauli algebra to `A_Gamma`. | External assumption/gap until the source construction is formalized. |\n| `main.tex:1927-1931` | Writes a pure/mixed product density state. | Finite density-matrix fragments are formalized; the infinite model is not. |\n| `main.tex:1945-1967` | Proposes the GNS/tensor-factor and type conclusions. | Conditional GNS transport is formalized; analytic product and type conclusions are not. |\n| `main.tex:1970-2004` | Proposes quasi-equivalence and normal-folium transport. | Not formalized. |\n\nThe wording above is a locator-oriented paraphrase, not a replacement for the\nmanuscript.\n\n## Permitted auxiliary assumptions\n\nAny manuscript-facing Lean theorem that needs one of the following must expose\nit in the theorem statement or task packet:\n\n1. a completed C-star or von Neumann algebra model for the infinite Pauli\n   system and its regional algebra;\n2. the asserted star-isomorphism from that model to the regional algebra;\n3. the product-state formula and hypotheses making the GNS representation a\n   spatial tensor product;\n4. the von Neumann closure, normality, and quasi-equivalence assumptions needed\n   to transport the claimed factor type; and\n5. any hyperfiniteness or trace theorem used for the core factor.\n\nNone of these assumptions is supplied merely by the phrase “short-range\norder” in the current manuscript source.\n\n## Trace correction\n\nThe manuscript-facing target must distinguish two cases:\n\n- if the pure-sector Hilbert space is finite-dimensional, a normalized tracial\n  state can be obtained from the finite matrix trace together with the core\n  trace;\n- if the pure-sector Hilbert space is infinite-dimensional, the appropriate\n  conclusion is a faithful normal semifinite trace/weight on the `II_infinity`\n  target, not a tracial state.\n\nThis is a correction to the intended theorem contract, not a claim that the\ncurrent manuscript already states or proves the corrected dichotomy.\n\n## Legacy firewall\n\nEarlier gLU/refinement/layer-coherence material is listed in\n`CONTEXT-LEDGER.md`. It is retained, but it is neither a source clause nor an\nimplicit assumption of this formalization.\n# P53 closeout review — local-hyperbolic algebraic alpha\n\n## Decision\n\n**Status: proved at the stated conditional Lane-H scope; queue may advance.**\n\nThe completed Aristotle project for task\n`11e84c2b-b0a0-420f-ac80-d38a8a5695bb` was downloaded to\n`aristotle_responses/P53-local-hyperbolic-algebraic-alpha.tar.gz`\n(SHA-256\n`89df64accdc83453c13fe7a5a9c6080b80811a3df44947576b0d9e342a100a4f`)\nand extracted, without a build, update, or dependency fetch, under\n`aristotle_responses/P53-quarantine/`. Only the packet-authorized module\n`AristotleCandidates/LocalHyperbolicAlgebraicAlpha.lean` was integrated into\nthe live project. Its quarantine and live SHA-256 values agree:\n`797dd652c0cef03fd6481aee5331446fdad4dba7f4db9f310bda6d6b76efcd1b`.\nThe archive, extraction, and `ARISTOTLE_SUMMARY.md` remain raw response\nrecords; no other candidate module was copied.\n\n## Exact declarations and assumptions\n\nThe module defines the concrete finite twisted-Pauli-word algebra\n`pauliAlgebra`, its word basis `pauliWordBasis`, the coordinate pairing\n`coordPairing`, and `AlphaData`. Under `AlphaData A`, the load-bearing\ndeclarations are:\n\n- `stageLabelMap_bijective`: every finite-stage label map is a bijection;\n- `stage_mulCompatible` and `stage_starCompatible`: the explicitly defined\n  quadratic phase satisfies the word multiplication and involution equations;\n- `stage`: a constructed `FiniteAdaptedCoordinateStarData`, with no supplied\n  finite-stage `StarAlgEquiv` field;\n- `directedFamily`: the coherent finite-stage system;\n- `alpha`: the resulting algebraic direct-limit `StarAlgEquiv`;\n- `alpha_word`, `alpha_zWord`, `alpha_xWord`, `alpha_symm_word`, and\n  `existsUnique_alpha`: the phase-calibrated word and inverse formulas and\n  uniqueness; and\n- `standardAlphaData`: a tautological non-vacuity witness on `Nat`.\n\nThe conditional premises are explicit fields of `AlphaData`:\n\n1. P52's `LocalHyperbolicFamily.indep` and `LatticeExhaustion` data;\n2. `[LinearOrder I]`, used solely for the quadratic-phase ordering convention;\n3. `symplectic`, equality of the antisymmetrized source and target Pauli\n   pairings; and\n4. `stage_surjective`, onto-ness of each finite source-label block onto its\n   regional target-label block.\n\nP52 already proves injectivity and inclusion coherence. P53 derives stage\nbijectivity by combining that proof with `stage_surjective`; it does not hide\nstage equivalences, phase calibration, or whole-stage coherence in fields.\nThe local `symplectic` and `stage_surjective` conditions are additional\nauxiliary assumptions, not consequences established from the manuscript in\nthis repository.\n\n## Acceptance review\n\n| Classification | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| proved | From the named P52 data plus `symplectic` and `stage_surjective`, P53 constructs the finite twisted Pauli algebras, phase-calibrated finite-stage star equivalences, commuting directed system, and algebraic direct-limit star equivalence `alpha`. |\n| partial | The manuscript specialization is conditional: the repository does not construct the actual regional symplectic-coordinate realization or prove the stage-surjectivity premise from the cited manuscript clauses. The formula on generators is phase-calibrated, not an unphased literal equality. |\n| blocked | No obstruction blocks this algebraic gate. The next gates—concrete C-star realization/extension, product-state identity, GNS spatial tensor splitting, factorhood, and trace/weight classification—remain P54--P59 work. |\n| failed | None. |\n\nThe packet's mathematical target is met at its stated conditional scope. The\nalternative route builds a project-local finite twisted-word algebra rather\nthan assuming stage equivalences. This adds precisely `symplectic` and\n`stage_surjective` as premises; it does not weaken the requested conclusion.\n\n## Plan alignment\n\n- **Package and lane:** P53, Lane H.\n- **Predecessors:** P52 is integrated, compiled, and locally audited in\n  `reviews/P52-coherent-local-hyperbolic-coordinates-closeout.md`. The module\n  imports P52 plus checked phase/coherence/direct-limit infrastructure; it\n  imports no later P54--P61 package.\n- **Permitted gate:** discharged: constructed phase-calibrated finite-stage\n  star equivalences, their coherent algebraic direct-limit equivalence, and\n  the direct-limit `alpha` word formulas.\n- **Forbidden downstream claims:** respected. The module explicitly makes no\n  C-star completion, state identity, GNS tensor split, spatial tensor-product,\n  factorhood, trace, or weight theorem, and no such declaration occurs.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates/LocalHyperbolicAlgebraicAlpha.lean` — passed\n  in the live project (8045 jobs); no build ran in quarantine.\n- `lake build` — passed in the live project.\n- `lake env lean /dev/stdin` with `#print axioms` for\n  `stageLabelMap_bijective`, `stage_mulCompatible`, `stage_starCompatible`,\n  `directedFamily`, `alpha`, `alpha_word`, `alpha_zWord`, `alpha_xWord`,\n  `existsUnique_alpha`, and `standardAlphaData` — each reports only\n  `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`.\n- Placeholder scan across the candidate and its direct P52/phase/direct-limit\n  imports — no `sorry`, `admit`, user `axiom`, `opaque`, `unsafe`,\n  `implemented_by`, or `native_decide` occurrence.\n- Quarantine/live SHA-256 comparison and `git diff --check` — passed.\n\n## Adversarial review\n\nNo acceptance-blocking finding. The review checked that finite-stage\nsurjectivity is exposed rather than inferred from P52, that symmetry of the\ndiscrepancy is obtained only from the named symplectic premise, that the\nquadratic phase is used in both multiplication and star compatibility, and\nthat `alpha_zWord`/`alpha_xWord` retain the phase. Compilation validates the\nformal conditional construction; it does not establish the manuscript's\ngeometric realization or any later analytic/operator-algebraic statement.\n\n## Cleanup and worktree state\n\nKept intentionally: the integrated P53 candidate, its response archive,\nquarantine extraction, and this review. Pre-existing untracked P49/P49A/P49B\ncandidate and review files remain untouched. No manuscript file was changed;\nno commit, push, dependency update, archive build, or dependency fetch was\nperformed.\n# P58 closeout review — mixed UHF factor classification\n\n## Decision\n\n**Status: proved at the stated mixed-sector, conditional Lane-H scope; queue may\nadvance.**\n\nAristotle task `ed55ef94-0313-4123-9cc0-b00ffdb465aa` was downloaded as\n`aristotle_responses/P58-mixed-uhf-hyperfinite-factor.tar.gz` (SHA-256\n`6a9c6e453986cbacfed106b03db592f946fd61c13acb976a9b9da8f4c3c7c7b5`) and\nextracted without building, updating, or fetching dependencies at\n`aristotle_responses/P58-quarantine/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p58-3px4hkyb_aristotle/`.\nOnly the packet-authorized module\n`AristotleCandidates/MixedUHFHyperfiniteFactor.lean` was integrated into the\nlive project. Its quarantine and live SHA-256 values agree:\n`5dbf9ff8c35035c94b37804435793102cb0c59f88c7a39e2746c32274fc67d20`.\nThe archive and extraction remain raw response records. No manuscript file was\nchanged.\n\n## Source and exact declarations\n\nThe source basis is the narrow claim in `main.tex:1945-1967`, specifically the\nfinite maximally-mixed matrix alternative and the infinite maximally-mixed\nhyperfinite-II1 assertion at lines 1964-1966. This packet formalizes only the\nproject-local dyadic mixed sector; it neither establishes the preceding GNS\ntensor splitting nor transports its result to the manuscript's regional algebra.\n\nThe new module's load-bearing declarations are:\n\n- `qubitMatrixStarEquiv` (line 197) and\n  `qubitTensorTrace_eq_normalizedTrace` (line 213), identifying the `n`-qubit\n  algebra with `M_(2^n)(C)` and its trace with normalized matrix trace;\n- `qubitTensorPower_isMixedMatrixFactor` (line 291), whose explicit fields are\n  the star equivalence, positivity of `2^n`, normalized-trace identity,\n  traciality, faithfulness, and algebraic scalar centre;\n- `qubitUHF_hasScalarCenter` (line 314) and\n  `qubitUHF_not_matrixAlgebra` (line 331), the algebraic infinite-limit\n  statements;\n- `uhfConcreteCStar_isMatricialChain` (line 410), an increasing dense chain of\n  finite matrix subalgebras in the P54 concrete C-star model;\n- `matrixRange_vonNeumannGenerated_trivialCenter` (line 683) and\n  `mixedStage_vonNeumannGenerated_trivialCenter` (line 725), direct\n  matrix-unit proofs of trivial centre for each finite-stage generated concrete\n  von Neumann algebra;\n- `mixedVonNeumann` (line 739), defined as the von Neumann algebra generated\n  by `UHFConcreteCStar`; and\n- the conditional `mixedVonNeumann_isHyperfiniteFiniteFactor` (line 840).\n\nThe last theorem uses exactly the three fields of\n`MixedWeakClosurePremises` (lines 798-811): traciality of `uhfVectorState` on\nthe weak closure, faithfulness there, and `HasTrivialOperatorCenter` of that\nweak closure. `IsHyperfiniteFiniteFactorModel` (line 814) is explicitly a\nproject-local feature predicate: factorhood, a vector-normal faithful tracial\nstate, a matricial chain, and unbounded matrix sizes. It is **not** a proof of\nthe Murray-von Neumann/Connes uniqueness/classification theorem for the\nhyperfinite II1 factor.\n\n## Acceptance review\n\n| Classification | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| proved | The finite mixed stage is star-isomorphic to `M_(2^n)(C)` with normalized faithful tracial functional and scalar centre. The algebraic UHF limit has scalar centre and is not a finite matrix algebra. In the P54 representation, finite matrix stages form a monotone dense C-star-level chain; each individual stage's generated von Neumann algebra has trivial centre by the local matrix-unit proof. The conditional theorem assembles the stated project-local finite-factor model. |\n| partial | Infinite weak-closure traciality, faithfulness, and factorhood are not proved; they are the three named fields above. The module's `IsVectorNormal` is a project-local single-vector-functional predicate, not a formalized Mathlib sigma-weak continuity theory. No canonical hyperfinite-II1 classification/isomorphism is formalized. |\n| blocked | Nothing blocks P58's stated gate, because the packet expressly permits an analytic factoriality/classification bridge only as an explicit conditional interface. Those analytic premises remain open for any later use. |\n| failed | None. |\n\nThe packet's mathematical target is met at its stated scope. The alternate\nroute is a direct finite-matrix/matrix-unit construction plus a C-star-level\nmatricial approximation, rather than an unproved weak-closure transfer. It\nadds exactly the three `MixedWeakClosurePremises`; it does not silently weaken\nthe finite result or promote the conditional infinite result to a theorem of\nthe manuscript.\n\n## Plan alignment\n\n- **Package and lane:** P58, Lane H — correct.\n- **Predecessors:** P54 is integrated, compiled, and audited in\n  `reviews/P54-uhf-reference-representation-closeout.md`. The imports\n  `Formalization.DyadicTensorTower`, P54's\n  `UHFReferenceRepresentation`, and the pre-existing local bicommutant core\n  are byte-identical between the quarantine snapshot and live checkout. The\n  bicommutant core is supporting infrastructure, not an undeclared later Lane-H\n  package dependency.\n- **Permitted gate:** discharged: the finite mixed matrix alternative is\n  proved, and the infinite alternative supplies a checked matrix approximation\n  with all weak-closure/factor/classification gaps isolated as named premises.\n- **Forbidden downstream claims:** respected. The candidate contains no\n  regional alpha transport, pure-sector classification, spatial product\n  factorhood, regional factor claim, or final trace/weight theorem. Its\n  finite-stage factor statements and conditional mixed weak-closure model are\n  confined to the P54 dyadic reference representation.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates.MixedUHFHyperfiniteFactor` — passed (8038\n  jobs) in the live project.\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates.UHFReferenceRepresentation AristotleCandidates.BicommutantVonNeumannCore AristotleCandidates.MixedUHFHyperfiniteFactor Formalization` — passed (8089 jobs) in the live project.\n- `lake build` — passed in the live project; no work was required after the\n  focused build.\n- `lake env lean -o .lake/build/lib/lean/AristotleCandidates/MixedUHFHyperfiniteFactor.olean AristotleCandidates/MixedUHFHyperfiniteFactor.lean` — passed in the live project, producing the importable cache used by the axiom check.\n- `#print axioms` for `qubitTensorPower_isMixedMatrixFactor`,\n  `qubitUHF_hasScalarCenter`, `qubitUHF_not_matrixAlgebra`,\n  `uhfConcreteCStar_isMatricialChain`,\n  `matrixRange_vonNeumannGenerated_trivialCenter`,\n  `mixedStage_vonNeumannGenerated_trivialCenter`,\n  `uhfVectorState_isVectorNormal`, and\n  `mixedVonNeumann_isHyperfiniteFiniteFactor` — each reports only\n  `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`.\n- Forbidden-declaration scan of the candidate and its three direct imports —\n  no `sorry`, `admit`, user `axiom`, `opaque`, `unsafe`,\n  `implemented_by`, or `native_decide` occurrence.\n- Direct-import SHA-256 comparisons, candidate quarantine/live SHA-256\n  comparison, and `git diff --check` — passed.\n\n## Adversarial review\n\nNo acceptance-blocking finding. The review checked the finite normalization\nagainst the actual recursive matrix equivalence; that the algebraic scalar-\ncentre proof first reduces an arbitrary limit element to a finite stage; that\nthe non-matrix result uses a finite-rank obstruction rather than a mere label;\nand that the matrix-unit proof establishes only trivial centre for each finite\ngenerated algebra. It also checked that `mixedVonNeumann` factorhood,\nfaithfulness, and traciality remain three separate explicit premises, and that\nthe project-local `IsHyperfiniteFiniteFactorModel` is not reported as a\nhyperfinite-II1 uniqueness theorem. Lean builds and axiom reports validate the\nformal statements, not the manuscript's unformalized GNS tensor splitting or\nthe open analytic closure bridge.\n\n## Cleanup and worktree state\n\nKept intentionally: the P58 candidate, this closeout review, its raw archive,\nquarantine extraction, and the generated `.olean` under the existing\n`.lake/build/` cache. All previously untracked P49/P49A/P49B/P53 candidates\nand reviews remain untouched. No commit, push, dependency update, archive\nbuild, fetch, or manuscript modification was performed.\nFORMALIZATION-AUDIT-DECISION.md\nFORMALIZATION-SEMANTIC-AUDIT.md\nTWO-LANE-FORMALIZATION-DECISION.md\n\n-- task log --\nID                                   CREATED              NAME                           STATUS         \n---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n2e89017e-ccab-47c2-bd66-ca42164fd972 1 hour ago           # Autonomous proof-developm... COMPLETE       \n\n-- archive members --\naristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p55a-40elnrcu_aristotle/lakefile.lean\naristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p55a-40elnrcu_aristotle/Formalization.lean\naristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p55a-40elnrcu_aristotle/lean-toolchain\naristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p55a-40elnrcu_aristotle/lake-manifest.json\naristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p55a-40elnrcu_aristotle/AristotleCandidates/DensityPartialTrace.lean\naristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p55a-40elnrcu_aristotle/AristotleCandidates/ProductFactorClassificationBoundary.lean\naristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p55a-40elnrcu_aristotle/AristotleCandidates/KaplanskyDensity.lean\naristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p55a-40elnrcu_aristotle/AristotleCandidates/FiniteCornerTrace.lean\naristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p55a-40elnrcu_aristotle/AristotleCandidates/AlgebraicLimitOperatorRepresentation.lean\naristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p55a-40elnrcu_aristotle/AristotleCandidates/GeneralLatticeProjectionTower.lean\naristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p55a-40elnrcu_aristotle/AristotleCandidates/NormalFaithfulCornerTrace.lean\naristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p55a-40elnrcu_aristotl