{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,300p' <original-home>/.codex/adversarial_review.md && sed -n '1,320p' work/FORMALIZATION-SEMANTIC-AUDIT.md && sed -n '1,260p' work/FORMALIZATION-AUDIT-DECISION.md && sed -n '1,260p' reviews/P54-uhf-reference-representation-closeout.md && git status --short\"","aggregated_output":"# Adversarial Review Protocol\n\nUse this before closing substantive Codex work. The goal is to find defects, not\nto summarize accomplishments.\n\n## Scope\n\n1. Identify the artifact types touched: `code`, `math`, `tex`, `computation`,\n   `source-backed`, `workflow`.\n2. Inspect the diff or new artifact against the user's request.\n3. Report findings by severity first. If there are no findings, say so and state\n   the remaining risk.\n\n## Universal Checks\n\n- Did the work answer the actual latest user request?\n- Did it modify unrelated files or broaden scope?\n- Did it overwrite, reformat, or revert pre-existing user changes?\n- Are generated files, caches, logs, plots, PDFs, or build artifacts handled\n  intentionally?\n- Are final claims stronger than the evidence supports?\n- Are verification commands actually relevant to the changed artifact?\n\n## Code Checks\n\n- Does the changed behavior match the stated interface and edge cases?\n- Are tests missing for a changed behavior, bug fix, parser, numerical routine,\n  CLI command, or user-facing workflow?\n- Are errors handled where inputs, files, network calls, or external tools can\n  fail?\n- Is there hidden global state, path sensitivity, nondeterminism, race risk, or\n  stale cache behavior?\n- Did dependency, config, or environment changes alter unrelated workflows?\n\n## Math Checks\n\n- Are all assumptions, domains, signs, conventions, normalizations, and boundary\n  conditions stated before use?\n- Are definitions used consistently throughout the derivation?\n- Is any implication actually reversible, or was a one-way statement used both\n  ways?\n- Are there division-by-zero, invertibility, regularity, convergence, branch-cut,\n  gauge, or boundary-term assumptions?\n- Do limiting cases, dimensions/units, symmetries, and known special cases agree?\n- Are symbolic substitutions justified rather than smuggling in the result?\n- Are claims labeled correctly as proof, derivation, check, conjecture, or\n  numerical evidence?\n\n## TeX And Source-Backed Checks\n\n- Does the document compile if compilation was expected?\n- Are labels, references, citations, bibliography entries, and figure paths valid?\n- Are source-backed claims tied to exact locators when required?\n- Is quoted or paraphrased material clearly separated from the agent's synthesis?\n- Does the exposition define terms before using them in load-bearing statements?\n\n## Computation Checks\n\n- Is the computation reproducible from a recorded command?\n- Are inputs, random seeds, versions, tolerances, and units documented when they\n  affect the result?\n- Are outputs interpreted correctly and not over-promoted beyond the computation?\n- Were independent sanity checks used where feasible: small cases, limiting\n  cases, dimensional analysis, symbolic identities, or alternate algorithms?\n\n## Closeout Template\n\nUse this structure internally, then surface the concise version to the user:\n\n```text\nFindings:\n- [severity] file/path:line - issue and consequence.\n\nChecks run:\n- command -> result.\n\nResidual risk:\n- what was not checked, or why the artifact is not a proof/complete validation.\n\nCleanup:\n- remaining dirty/untracked files and whether they are intentional.\n```\n# Formalization semantic audit\n\nStatus: first inventory in progress.\n\nThis document is the approved semantic/tutorial audit described in\n`FORMALIZATION-AUDIT-DECISION.md`. It is not itself a proof and does not\nchange the manuscript theorem status.\n\n## Audit verdict convention\n\n- **proved**: the stated Lean theorem follows from its explicit hypotheses and\n  compiles without placeholders;\n- **conditional**: the Lean implication is proved, but one or more hypotheses\n  are supplied structures or external analytic assumptions;\n- **infrastructure**: reusable Lean mathematics with no manuscript claim;\n- **unformalized**: a manuscript step for which no corresponding theorem is\n  currently present;\n- **not aligned**: the Lean conclusion is stronger, weaker, or materially\n  different from the natural-language sentence.\n\nCompilation, axiom reports, and mathematical alignment will be recorded\nseparately.\n\n## Source clauses\n\nThe manuscript-facing audit uses only the locators recorded in\n`SOURCE-CONTRACT.md`:\n\n- `main.tex:1671-1679`: local symplectic basis and finite-support condition;\n- `main.tex:1740-1752`: regional factor theorem statement;\n- `main.tex:1915-1920`: proposed adapted-basis star-isomorphism;\n- `main.tex:1927-1931`: pure/mixed product density state;\n- `main.tex:1945-1967`: GNS, tensor, and factor claims;\n- `main.tex:1970-2004`: quasi-equivalence and normal-folium claims.\n\n## Initial module inventory\n\nThe detailed theorem ledger and dependency graph are the next sections to be\nfilled after inspecting the principal declarations. The current theorem\ncontract itself still says:\n\n```lean\ndef regionalAlgebraTheoremStatus : String :=\n  \"conditional contract pending analytic model\"\n```\n\nThat status is consistent with the source contract and is not to be upgraded\nwithout discharging the missing finite-coordinate, representation, normality,\nand product-classification premises.\n\n## First-pass verdict\n\nThe current formalization is a sequence of conditional bridges, not yet a\nformal proof of the manuscript's regional factor theorem. The strongest\ncurrently checked route is:\n\n```text\nfinite adapted-coordinate data\n  -> finite StarAlgEquiv at each stage\n  -> coherent algebraic direct-limit StarAlgEquiv alpha\n  -> compatible algebraic state transport\n  -> supplied compatible operator representation\n  -> closed operator-range C*-algebra\n  -> supplied state-preserving C*-extension\n  -> GNS unitary and algebraic bicommutant transport\n  -> conditional product-factor/type classification\n```\n\nThe arrows are not all existence theorems. In particular, the source-specific\nfinite coordinate realization, a faithful representation of the algebraic\nlimit, the regional C*-extension, the analytic normality/WOT statements, and\nthe product-factor classification remain explicit premises or missing\nmathematics.\n\n## Status table for the reviewed overnight packages\n\n| Package | Principal Lean object | Semantic verdict | Main external premise |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| P37 | `algebraicLimitOperatorRep` | conditional theorem proved | compatible finite-stage operator representations |\n| P38 | `quasilocalCStarAlgebra` | conditional theorem proved | supplied compatible representation; stage injectivity for faithfulness |\n| P39 | `StatePreservingData`, `gnsUnitary` | conditional theorem proved | C*-completion, alpha extension, state identity and continuity |\n| P40 | `bicommutantStarEquiv`, folium transport | algebraic part proved; analytic part conditional | WOT/double-commutant and normal-functional characterizations |\n| P41 | `ProductGNSFactorization` | partial boundary only | supplied factorization/classification; infinite weight interface is incomplete |\n| P42--P46 | no reviewed candidate currently present | not yet audited | candidate/archive status must be established before use |\n\nAll five reviewed packages compile in the local project. Their closeout\nreviews explicitly separate compilation from mathematical scope. P41 is\naccepted only as partial: its infinite-pure `TracialWeightCore` does not yet\nassert positivity, normality, faithfulness, or semifiniteness.\n\n## Dependency spine and one-to-one theorem anchors\n\n### 1. Finite coordinate map\n\nNatural-language sentence:\n\n> Given finite adapted source and target word bases, send each source word to a\n> phase-corrected target word.\n\nLean anchor:\n\n```lean\nFiniteAdaptedCoordinateStarData.starEquiv\nFiniteAdaptedCoordinateStarData.starEquiv_word\nFiniteAdaptedCoordinateStarData.starEquiv_correctedWord\n```\n\nSemantic status: the construction is proved from the fields of\n`FiniteAdaptedCoordinateStarData`, but the actual manuscript-specific finite\ndata are not constructed from `main.tex:1671-1679` or `main.tex:1915-1920`.\n\n### 2. Coherence of finite maps\n\nNatural-language sentence:\n\n> The finite coordinate maps commute with the inclusions of stages.\n\nLean anchor:\n\n```lean\nstarEquiv_connecting_of_pauliBasis\nDirectedFiniteCoordinateFamily.stageEquiv_connecting\n```\n\nSemantic status: proved when word, label, phase, and connecting-map\ncompatibility are supplied.\n\n### 3. Algebraic infinite map\n\nNatural-language sentence:\n\n> Compatible finite maps descend to a unique star-isomorphism of algebraic\n> direct limits.\n\nLean anchor:\n\n```lean\nDirectedFiniteCoordinateFamily.alpha\nDirectedFiniteCoordinateFamily.alpha_of\nDirectedFiniteCoordinateFamily.existsUnique_alpha\n```\n\nSemantic status: this is a genuine algebraic direct-limit theorem, conditional\non the finite coherent family. It is not yet a C*-completion theorem.\n\n### 4. State transport\n\nNatural-language sentence:\n\n> Pull the target product state back along the algebraic alpha.\n\nLean anchor:\n\n```lean\nTargetStageStates.targetLimitState\nTargetStageStates.pulledBackState\nTargetStageStates.pulledBackState_eq_targetLimitState_alpha\nTargetStageStates.pulledBackState_isAlgebraicState\n```\n\nSemantic status: the state-level implication is proved from compatible target\nstage states. The infinite product density operator itself is not constructed\nas a von Neumann-algebraic state in this module.\n\n### 5. Algebraic operator representation\n\nNatural-language sentence:\n\n> Compatible finite-stage operator representations define a representation of\n> the quasi-local algebra.\n\nLean anchor:\n\n```lean\nalgebraicLimitOperatorRep\nalgebraicLimitOperatorRep_of\nalgebraicLimitOperatorRep_stage_congr\nalgebraicLimitOperatorRep_injective\n```\n\nSemantic status: proved conditionally. Injectivity requires stagewise\ninjectivity; no infinite tensor-product Hilbert space is constructed.\n\n### 6. Concrete C*-model\n\nNatural-language sentence:\n\n> Complete the quasi-local algebra in the operator norm.\n\nLean anchor:\n\n```lean\nOperatorRepresentation.rangeClosure\nOperatorRepresentation.embedding\nOperatorRepresentation.denseRange_embedding\n```\n\nand, for the direct-limit range,\n\n```lean\nquasilocalCStarAlgebra\nquasilocalEmbedding\ndenseRange_quasilocalEmbedding\n```\n\nSemantic status: the closure is genuinely constructed inside bounded\noperators, but only after an isometric operator representation is supplied.\nThis does not prove that the manuscript's algebra has such a representation.\n\n### 7. State-preserving GNS transport\n\nNatural-language sentence:\n\n> A state-preserving C*-isomorphism induces a canonical GNS unitary.\n\nLean anchor:\n\n```lean\nStatePreservingData.sourceState_eq_pullback\nStatePreservingData.gnsUnitary\nStatePreservingData.gnsUnitary_intertwines\nStatePreservingData.gnsConjStarAlgEquiv\n```\n\nSemantic status: proved from supplied C*-completions, state positivity/order\ndata, continuity, and an exact state identity. It is not a proof of the\nmanuscript's state identity.\n\n### 8. Bicommutant transport\n\nNatural-language sentence:\n\n> The GNS unitary identifies the represented von Neumann algebras.\n\nLean anchors:\n\n```lean\nStarSubalgebra.vonNeumannGenerated\nStarSubalgebra.le_vonNeumannGenerated\nStarSubalgebra.vonNeumannGenerated_le\nbicommutantStarEquiv_sourceRepVN\n```\n\nSemantic status: the algebraic bicommutant/conjugation statement is proved.\nThe identification with strong/weak operator closure and the normal-folium\nstep are conditional interfaces, not proved analytic theorems.\n\n### 9. Product-factor and trace conclusion\n\nNatural-language sentence:\n\n> The product GNS algebra is a type-I pure factor tensor a finite type-I or\n> hyperfinite type-II1 mixed factor, with the appropriate trace conclusion.\n\nLean anchors:\n\n```lean cddddddddssssssssssssssssssssssssssw1\nProductGNSFactorization.pureFactor_typeI_of_finite\nProductGNSFactorization.pureFactor_typeIInfinity_of_infinite\nProductGNSFactorization.mixedFactor_typeI_of_finite\nProductGNSFactorization.mixedFactor_hyperfiniteII1_of_infinite\nfinitePureSector_product_classification\ninfinitePureSector_product_classification\n```\n\nSemantic status: the type labels and tensor identification are supplied data.\nThe finite algebraic trace transport is proved. The infinite-pure package does\nnot yet provide a faithful normal semifinite weight, so the corrected\ninfinite-sector trace conclusion is not formalized.\n# Formalization semantic-audit decision\n\nDate: 2026-08-07\n\nThe approved deliverable is a semantic audit/tutorial of the Lean\nformalization, rather than another proof package or a compilation report.\n\nThe audit will provide:\n\n1. a status summary separating proved mathematics, conditional interfaces,\n   supplied data, and unformalized claims;\n2. a dependency map from the manuscript's finite-coordinate argument through\n   the algebraic limit, concrete C-star model, GNS transport, bicommutant\n   transport, and product-factor boundary;\n3. a theorem ledger mapping each important natural-language proof sentence to\n   exact Lean declarations, hypotheses, intermediate lemmas, and semantic\n   verdicts; and\n4. a step-by-step Lean reading sequence with code excerpts and direct build or\n   `#check` commands.\n\nThe audit must keep compilation separate from mathematical validity and must\nidentify exact manuscript locators from `SOURCE-CONTRACT.md`. In particular,\nit must not call the regional hyperfinite-factor theorem proved merely because\nconditional Lean interfaces compile.\n\nThe first pass will inventory the current modules and completed-package\nreviews. Later passes will inspect the principal declarations and their proof\nchains in dependency order.\n# P54 closeout review — faithful UHF reference representation\n\n## Decision\n\n**Status: proved at the stated infrastructure-only Lane-H scope; queue may\nadvance.**\n\nThe completed Aristotle project was downloaded as\n`aristotle_responses/P54-uhf-reference-representation.tar.gz` (SHA-256\n`2843359fff4021ff2350373fd8ec82c3ffd0948ccf723193b5bc996a0d084668`) and\nextracted, without building, updating, or fetching dependencies, at\n`aristotle_responses/P54-extracted/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p54-0ps3ce65_aristotle/`.\nOnly the packet-authorized module\n`AristotleCandidates/UHFReferenceRepresentation.lean` was integrated into the\nlive project.  Its SHA-256 is\n`786a1b2b89bf14eb61cf7f703ea646d095d3d640ac20b814c012a6e82b1c8eb9` in both\nlocations.  The archive and extraction remain raw response records.\n\n## Exact declarations and assumptions\n\nThe module imports only the pre-existing, byte-identical live modules\n`Formalization.DyadicTensorTower`,\n`AristotleCandidates.AlgebraicLimitOperatorRepresentation`, and\n`AristotleCandidates.ConcreteCStarCompletion`.\n\nIt constructs the following principal declarations:\n\n- `UHFL2`, `uhfL2Core`, and `UHFGNS`, the trace-GNS pre-Hilbert space of\n  `QubitUHFAlgebra` and its `UniformSpace.Completion`;\n- `qubitTensorPower_exists_bound`, `qubitUHF_exists_bound`,\n  `qubitUHFTrace_faithful`, and `uhfNormSq_mul_le`;\n- `uhfRep : QubitUHFAlgebra →⋆ₐ[ℂ] (UHFGNS →L[ℂ] UHFGNS)`, together with\n  `uhfRep_injective`, `uhfCyclicVector_norm`, and\n  `uhfRep_vector_state`;\n- the compatible finite-stage family `uhfStageRep` and\n  `uhfRepData : QubitOperatorRepresentationData UHFGNS`, with\n  `uhfStageRep_compat`, `uhfRepData_rho_injective`,\n  `uhfRepData_limitRep`, and `uhfRepData_limitRep_injective`; and\n- the concrete closed operator-range C-star algebra `UHFConcreteCStar` with\n  its injective dense embedding `uhfConcreteEmbedding` and\n  `uhfConcreteEmbedding_denseRange`.\n\nThere are **no supplied auxiliary assumptions**: boundedness is established\nfrom the internal algebraic sum-of-squares cone `sumSqCone` and the finite\ndyadic matrix tower; faithfulness comes from the constructed canonical trace.\nThe Hilbert space is a completion of that pre-Hilbert space, not an assumed\ninfinite tensor-product Hilbert space.\n\n## Acceptance review\n\n| Classification | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| proved | The module constructs a faithful compatible Hilbert/operator representation of the algebraic dyadic limit, including injective finite-stage representations and the induced-limit identification. |\n| partial | The concrete closure is an operator-range C-star model, but P54 deliberately does not identify it with a project-specific regional completion or prove a spatial tensor-product model. |\n| blocked | Nothing blocks the P54 gate. |\n| failed | None. |\n\nThe packet's mathematical target is met at its stated scope.  The additional\nclosed operator-range C-star construction is supporting infrastructure and\ndoes not weaken or replace the requested faithful reference representation.\n\n## Plan alignment\n\n- **Package and lane:** P54, Lane H.\n- **Predecessors:** none.  The packet is one of the four explicitly approved\n  independent foundation packages.  Its three imports are prior local\n  infrastructure, not P47--P61 dependencies, and were byte-identical in the\n  quarantine snapshot and live checkout.\n- **Permitted gate:** discharged: a faithful compatible Hilbert/operator\n  representation of the dyadic algebraic limit is constructed from finite\n  stages, without assuming an infinite tensor-product Hilbert space.\n- **Forbidden downstream claims:** respected.  The candidate neither defines\n  a regional alpha nor proves a state identity for a regional algebra, a\n  spatial tensor product, factorhood/type, or a trace/weight classification.\n  Its trace-GNS vector-state identity concerns only the constructed dyadic\n  reference representation and is not such a classification claim.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates.UHFReferenceRepresentation` — passed in\n  the live project.\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates.UHFReferenceRepresentation Formalization`\n  — passed in the live project.\n- `lake build` — passed in the live project.\n- `lake env lean AristotleCandidates/UHFReferenceRepresentation.lean` —\n  passed.  Because the new untracked module was not emitted as an `.olean` by\n  the package target, the same live source was explicitly compiled with\n  `lake env lean -o .lake/build/lib/lean/AristotleCandidates/UHFReferenceRepresentation.olean ...`\n  before importing it for the axiom report.\n- `lake env lean /dev/stdin` with `#print axioms` for\n  `qubitTensorPower_exists_bound`, `qubitUHFTrace_faithful`,\n  `uhfNormSq_mul_le`, `uhfRep`, `uhfRep_injective`, `uhfStageRep_compat`,\n  `uhfRepData_limitRep_injective`, and `uhfConcreteEmbedding_denseRange` —\n  each reports only `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`.\n- Forbidden-declaration scan of the candidate and direct imports — no\n  `sorry`, `admit`, user `axiom`, `opaque`, `unsafe`, `implemented_by`, or\n  `native_decide` occurrence.  Quarantine/live SHA-256 comparison and\n  `git diff --check` — passed.\n\n## Adversarial review\n\nNo acceptance-blocking finding.  The review checked that the completion is\nexplicitly the trace-GNS completion rather than an infinite tensor product;\nthat the bounded left action is proved from the algebraic cone bound rather\nthan supplied as a completion/isometry interface; that the finite-stage\ncompatibility and limit faithfulness are actual declarations; and that the\ncandidate does not cross into P55--P59 regional, spatial, factor, or\ntrace/weight claims.  Lean compilation and axiom reports validate this\nformal infrastructure only; they do not establish any manuscript statement\nor later analytic tensor-factor conclusion.\n\n## Cleanup and worktree state\n\nKept intentionally: the integrated P54 candidate, the raw quarantine archive\nand extraction, this closeout review, and the generated live `.olean` cache\nunder the existing `.lake/build/` tree.  All pre-existing modified and\nuntracked work was preserved.  No manuscript file was changed; no commit,\npush, dependency update, archive build, or dependency fetch was performed.\n M PLAN.md\n M aristotle_tasks/P49-finite-corner-trace.md\n M aristotle_tasks/P50-normal-faithful-corner-trace.md\n M aristotle_tasks/P51-full-finite-corner-central-exclusion.md\n M aristotle_tasks/P55-regional-concrete-cstar-alpha.md\n M aristotle_tasks/P60-full-corner-semifinite-weight.md\n M work/TWO-LANE-FORMALIZATION-DECISION.md\n?? AristotleCandidates/FiniteCornerTrace.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/FullCornerSemifiniteWeight.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/FullFiniteCornerCentralExclusion.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/KaplanskyDensity.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/LocalHyperbolicAlgebraicAlpha.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/LocalHyperbolicFiniteStageUHFBridge.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/MixedUHFHyperfiniteFactor.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/NormalFaithfulCornerTrace.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/StrongOperatorClosedVonNeumann.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/UltraweakNormality.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/VonNeumannBicommutantTheorem.lean\n?? aristotle_tasks/P50U-ultraweak-normality-bridge.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P55A-local-hyperbolic-finite-stage-uhf-bridge.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P55B-local-hyperbolic-source-uhf-bridge.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P55C-local-hyperbolic-concrete-representations.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P55D-regional-concrete-cstar-alpha.md\n?? aristotle_tasks/P60R-full-corner-standard-semifiniteness-repair.md\n?? reviews/P49-finite-corner-trace-closeout.md\n?? reviews/P49-finite-corner-trace-recovery.md\n?? reviews/P49A-strong-operator-closed-von-neumann-closeout.md\n?? reviews/P49B-von-neumann-bicommutant-theorem-closeout.md\n?? reviews/P49C-kaplansky-density-closeout.md\n?? reviews/P50-normal-faithful-corner-trace-closeout-rerun.md\n?? reviews/P50-normal-faithful-corner-trace-closeout.md\n?? reviews/P50-normal-faithful-corner-trace-recovery.md\n?? reviews/P50U-ultraweak-normality-bridge-closeout.md\n?? reviews/P51-full-finite-corner-central-exclusion-closeout.md\n?? reviews/P51-full-finite-corner-central-exclusion-recovery.md\n?? reviews/P53-local-hyperbolic-algebraic-alpha-closeout.md\n?? reviews/P55-regional-concrete-cstar-alpha-out-of-budget.md\n?? reviews/P58-mixed-uhf-hyperfinite-factor-closeout.md\n?? reviews/P60-full-corner-semifinite-weight-closeout.md\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
